<title>VENEZUELA: Enron's Ventane 1st half net $540,000.</title>
<headline>Enron's Ventane 1st half net $540,000.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan affiliate of U.S. energy giant Enron Corp, Industrias Ventane SA, reported inflation-adjusted first half net profits for the period ending June 30 of 254 million bolivars ($540,000).</p>
<p>Comparative inflation adjusted 1995 results for Venezuela's leading liquid gas company, which is 80 percent owned by Enron, were not available, company treasurer Jesus Poleo told Reuters.</p>
<p>Total sales for the period were 9.9 billion bolivars, while costs of sales stood at 2.8 billion bolivars, operating costs at 6.0 billion bolivars, and exchange gains at 2.8 billion bolivars.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
